msgid "If yes, please answer the following questions with respect to the individual's generalised seizures. A generalised seizure is conceptualised as originating at some point within, and rapidly engaging, bilaterally distributed networks. Such bilateral networks can include cortical and subcortical structures, but do not necessarily include the entire cortex. Although individual seizure onsets can appear localised, the location and lateralisation are not consistent from one seizure to another. Generalised seizures can be asymmetric."
