msgid "<p>We’d like to collect more information on your child/adult with Angelman Syndrome’s seizure history from birth until now. If you are able to complete this section, please do so. Otherwise, we would be glad to contact your child/adult’s clinician on your behalf if you have provided consent to do this.</p>"
"\n"
"\n<p>If the individual has never experienced seizure activity you can move to the next module: Medications and Interventions</p>"
"\n"
"\n<p>If you require more information, please visit the following website:<a href=\"http://www.ilae.org/\"target=\"_blank\"><b>http://www.ilae.org/</b></a></p>"
"\n"
"\n<p><b>Please click the green 'Save' button before progressing to the next Module. </p></b>"
msgstr ""
msgid "Has your child/ adult ever experienced any seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What type of seizure was it?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Was it focal or generalised?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What do you think triggered the seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Has your child/ adult ever had any of the following seizure types?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Atonic Seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Seizures with sudden, brief loss of muscle tone of the body. The person will go limp and collapse, usually headfirst, so facial and head injuries are common. There may or may not be a brief loss of consciousness. Recovery is swift unless the person is injured. These seizures are also known as drop attacks."
msgstr ""

msgid "Age of onset"
msgstr ""

msgid "Is your child/ adult currently free from atonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Since their first atonic seizure, have they had periods of freedom from this type of seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What was their longest period of freedom from atonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Less than 6 months"
msgstr ""

msgid "6-12 months"
msgstr ""

msgid "12-24 months"
msgstr ""

msgid "More than 24 months"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been medicated for atonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been hospitalised for atonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Please comment on any other details about their atonic seizures (eg significant seizure events/ changes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tonic, Clonic or Tonic-Clonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tonic seizures - muscle tone is greatly increased and the body, arms, or legs make sudden stiffening movements. Duration is 3 seconds or greater."
"\nClonic seizures - consist of rhythmic jerking, movements of the arms and legs, sometimes on both sides of the body."
"\nTonic-clonic seizures - the person loses consciousness, muscles stiffen, and jerking movements are seen. Loss of urine or feces, tongue biting may occur."
msgstr ""
msgid "Is your child/ adult currently free from tonic, clonic and/or tonic-clonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Since their first tonic, clonic or tonic clonic seizure, have they had periods of freedom from this type of seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What was their longest period of freedom from tonic, clonic or tonic clonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been medicated for tonic, clonic, or tonic-clonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been hospitalised for tonic, clonic, or tonic-clonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Please comment on any other details about their tonic, clonic, or tonic-clonic seizures (eg significant seizure events/ changes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Myoclonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Seizures that are brief shock-like jerks of a muscle or group of muscles. Usually involving both sides of the body."
msgstr ""

msgid "Is your child/ adult currently free from myoclonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Since their first Myoclonic seizure, have they had periods of freedom from this type of seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What was their longest period of freedom from Myoclonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been medicated for myoclonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been hospitalised for myoclonic seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Please comment on any other details about their myoclonic seizures (eg significant seizure events/ changes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cluster motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "One episode of atonic, tonic, clonic or tonic-clonic seizures that are too many to count."
msgstr ""

msgid "Is your child/ adult currently free from cluster motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Since their first Cluster motor seizure, have they had periods of freedom from this type of seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What was their longest period of freedom from Cluster motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been medicated for cluster motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been hospitalised for cluster motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Please comment on any other details about their cluster motor seizures (eg significant seizure events/ changes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Absence seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Seizures that consist of short period of “blanking out” or staring into space. Duration typically 3 to 20 secs. Can be accompanied by automatisms or repeated automatic movements like clapping or rubbing of hands, lip smacking or chewing, or running. Previously called Petit Mal seizures."
msgstr ""

msgid "Is your child/ adult currently free from absence seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Since their first absence seizure, have they had periods of freedom from this type of seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What was their longest period of freedom from absence seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been medicated for absence seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been hospitalised for absence seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Please comment on any other details about their absence seizures (eg significant seizure events/ changes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cluster non-motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "One episode of absence seizures that are too many to count."
msgstr ""

msgid "Is your child/ adult currently free from cluster non motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Since their first cluster non motor seizure, have they had periods of freedom from this type of seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What was their longest period of freedom from cluster non motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been medicated for cluster non motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been hospitalised for cluster non motor seizures?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Please comment on any other details about their cluster non motor seizures (eg significant seizure events/ changes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Epileptic spasms?"
msgstr ""

msgid "An epileptic spasm is a sudden flexion, extension or mixed flexion-extension of proximal and truncal muscles, lasting 1-2 seconds i.e. longer than a myoclonic jerk (which lasts milliseconds) but not as long as a tonic seizure (which lasts > 2 seconds). Spasms typically occur in a series, usually on wakening. Subtle forms may occur with only chin movement, grimacing, or head nodding. Spasms may be bilaterally symmetric, asymmetric, or unilateral."
msgstr ""

msgid "Is your child/ adult currently free from epileptic spasms?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Since their first epileptic spasm, have they had periods of freedom from this type of seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What was their longest period of freedom from epileptic spasms?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been medicated for epileptic spasms?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been hospitalised for epileptic spasms?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Please comment on any other details about their epileptic spasms? (eg significant seizure events/ changes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Convulsive status epilepticus?"
msgstr ""

msgid "It follows a tonic-clonic seizure and one of the following conditions apply: a) The jerking portion of a tonic-clonic seizure last 5 minutes or longer; b) A person goes into a second seizure without recovering consciousness from the first one; c) A person has repeated seizures for 15 minutes or longer; d) This is usually a medical emergency. May be generalised or focal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Is your child/ adult currently free from convulsive status epilepticus?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Since their first episode of Convulsive status epilepticus, have they had periods of freedom from this type of seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What was their longest period of freedom from Convulsive status epilepticus?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been medicated for convulsive status epilepticus?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ever been hospitalised for convulsive status epilepticus?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Please comment on any other details about their convulsive status epilepticus (eg significant events/ changes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Non-convulsive status epilepticus?"
msgstr ""

msgid "It usually follows an absence seizure. The person may be confused or not fully aware of what is going on, but they are not “unconscious” like after a tonic-clonic seizure. Lasts more than 15 minutes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Is your child/ adult currently free from non convulsive status epilepticus?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Since their first episode of Non-convulsive status epilepticus, have they had periods of freedom from this type of seizure?"
msgstr ""

msgid "What was their longest period of freedom from Non-convulsive status epilepticus?"
msgstr ""

