msgid "<p>The next set of questions are about how your child communicated in specific situations over the past 30 days. If something is not applicable to your child, please select “No or only once”.</p>"
"\n<p><strong>Games could include peek-a-boo, chase, or catch. Activities could include swimming, playing with Play-Doh, or blocks.</strong></p>"
msgstr ""
msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child play at least one game or activity with you or others?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child anticipate at least one game or activity if you said the name out loud?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child indirectly ask to play at least one game or activity by starting to play the game/activity or by bringing you parts of the game/activity?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child ask to play at least one game or activity by name using a gesture/sign, word/word approximation, or symbol on a device?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child take turns when playing at least one game or activity?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, when he/she was playing, did your child pretend to do something?"
msgstr ""

msgid "15 - The next question is about how your child communicated in specific situations over the past 30 days."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child try to comfort someone if he/she noticed that he/she was upset?"
msgstr ""

msgid "16 - The next question is about how your child communicated in specific situations over the past 30 days."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, excluding times when he/she ignored you, did your child look at you or pause what he/she was doing when you said his/her name?"
msgstr ""

msgid "17 - Please tell us how your child responded to your directions."
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>The next set of questions are about how your child communicated in specific situations over the past 30 days. If something is not applicable to your child, please select “No or only once”.</p>"
"\n<p><strong>This first set of questions are about directions that are part of his/her daily routine. Please exclude times when your child may have ignored you.</strong></p>"
msgstr ""
msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child respond when you told him/her “no” or “stop”?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child follow one-step directions that are part of his/her daily routine? (example: “Get your cup” or “Let’s take a bath”)"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child follow two-step directions that are part of his/her daily routine? (example: \"Go to the kitchen and get your cup\")"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child follow three-step directions that are part of his/her daily routine? (example: \"Go inside, grab your shoes, and bring them to me\")"
msgstr ""

msgid "18 - Now, think about how your child responded to new directions."
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>The next set of questions are about how your child communicated in specific situations over the past 30 days. If something is not applicable to your child, please select “No or only once”.</p>"
"\n<p><strong>Please exclude times when your child may have ignored you.</strong></p>"
msgstr ""
msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child follow one-step directions that were new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child follow two-step directions that were new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child follow three-step directions that were new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "19 - The next question is about how your child communicated in specific situations over the past 30 days."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child understand your mood (example: angry, happy) based on your facial expression or tone of voice?"
msgstr ""

msgid "20 - Think about when you were talking to another person but not directly to your child."
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>The next question is about how your child communicated in specific situations over the past 30 days. If something is not applicable to your child, please select “No or only once”.</p>"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child show you that he/she understood isolated words or phrases that he/she overheard? (example: “grandma” or “television”)"
msgstr ""

msgid "21 - Think about how your child responded to questions."
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>The next set of questions are about how your child communicated in specific situations over the past 30 days. If something is not applicable to your child, please select “No or only once”.</p>"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, if you asked your child a question that had a “yes” or “no” response, did your child answer using a gesture/sign, word/word approximation, or a symbol on a device?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child answer open-ended questions? (example: \"What do you want to eat tonight?\"; \"Where do you want to go today?\")"
msgstr ""

msgid "22 - Think about when your child tried to tell you something, and how your child let you know if you understood him/her correctly."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, did your child let you know that you did not understand him/her correctly?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, if you did not understand your child, did your child try to communicate his/her message in a different way?"
msgstr ""

msgid "23 - The next set of questions are about how your child communicated in specific situations over the past 30 days."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, in general, were people familiar to your child (parents, teachers, caregivers, siblings) able to understand your child’s communication?"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the past 30 days, in general, were people less familiar to your child able to understand your child’s communication?"
msgstr ""

